Subject: [PATCH 3/3] mb/asrock/bc250: Add proof-of-life port of the ASRock
 BC-250

The bootblock prints the CPU name and CPUID, checks that the stock ABL
left an APOB at 0x4000000, and then halts, resets in a loop (for boards
without a serial console) or continues, depending on Kconfig. Reaching
the bootblock at all shows that the PSP accepted the image, trained
memory and handed control to coreboot.

The console defaults to the Super I/O COM1 that the stock DSDT
declares: a Nuvoton NCT6686D at 0x2E, logical device 2, 0x3F8, set up
with the NCT6687D code. The FCH UARTs remain selectable. Whether either
reaches a header on the board is not known yet.

